/tmp/arxiv2302.13657.t6eoSC/src/arxiv.tex:113:Loosely speaking, a homomorphism between two similar structures is a map that preserves relations, e.g., a graph homomorphism would be a map between the two graphs that preserves edges. Formally, a homomorphism is defined as follows.
