/tmp/arxiv2302.13657.t6eoSC/src/arxiv.tex:918:As before, vertices of $\Omega(\rel B)$ are tuples $U$ indexed by $V$-terms in $\trees$, where the $t$-th entry is a set of homomorphisms from $\Gamma(\relT t)$ to $\rel B$ such that $U_\vertex$ contains exactly one homomorphism. A difference here is that this homomorphism is the map $\emptyset \to B$, since $\Gamma(\relT \vertex)$ has no vertices as $\rel P \not\to \relT \vertex$.
