/tmp/arxiv2302.13657.t6eoSC/src/arxiv.tex:1190:\subsection{Proof of Theorem \ref{thm:adjoint-edge}}
/tmp/arxiv2302.13657.t6eoSC/src/arxiv.tex:1192:As noted above, the proof closely follows the proof of Theorem~\ref{thm:adjoint-1}, and we present it with the same structure starting with the easier of the two implications.
/tmp/arxiv2302.13657.t6eoSC/src/arxiv.tex:1194:The following lemma is an analogue to Lemma~\ref{lem:A-easy}. The statement is identical, although the meaning of $\Gamma$ and $\Omega$ has changed. In the proof, $h$ is no longer a homomorphism from $\Gamma(\relT t) \to \Gamma(\rel A)$, hence we replace every instance of $h$ being used as such a homomorphism with $h^{\check S}$.  Furthermore, to show that $g$ preserves an edge $e \in {\check S}^\rel A$, we need to provide a witness, which is $w_\bullet = f(e)$.
