+This is honestly Track B. The paper gives no distributional hardness theorem for planted homomorphisms—in fact its conclusion says no specific promise-CSP hardness application is known beyond the arc-graph use it cites—so Track A would be unsupported. The exact reference method enumerates the image of one source step and checks each possible multiplier: `O(m^2)`, with an eight-seed hard-preset median of 5,385 counted field operations and about 0.004 seconds. The compact route notices covariance of the set sum. The source set is constructed with sum one, so after summing both displayed sets the target sum is `u`; this is 238 modular additions at hard. The paper-side easy mechanism is functoriality itself (Section 6, before Definition 6.1), not a hardness theorem.
 
