codex
Implemented a self-contained Track B generator based on the paper’s Section 6.2 arc structures and induced homomorphisms. [The paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2302.13657v3) provides no distributional hardness result, so Track A would be unjustified.

Deliverables:

- [gen_2302_13657.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2302.13657/gen_2302_13657.py:23)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2302.13657/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2302.13657/README.md:1)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2302.13657/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2302.13657/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2302.13657/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- All G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- Guessing: 0/200,000; exact probability `1.999936e-7`.
- Five adversarial attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference method: 5,389 operations.
- Compact route: 242 operations.
- Witness: 31 characters, 6 atoms.

The result is not submit-ready: every mandatory oracle call returned HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded`, leaving zero scoreable attempts and no hardening verdict. The transcript files record those failures honestly. A funded `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is required to rerun STEP 4 and both G9 diagnostic arms.
